---
// Product page: Sessions. Built from design/Product Pages.dc.html (tab 0).
// The composite's illustrative metrics (< 100 ms, < 90 s, 4,000 kills,
// 41 MB, 1.2 GB, restored in 87s) are replaced by the measured
// equivalents in src/generated/proof.json, each with an evidence link.
import Product from './_Product.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';

const metrics = [
  {
    label: 'Kill-and-resume cycles',
    value: '25/25',
    note: 'fresh cycles; Wilson 95% CI [86.7%, 100.0%]',
    badge: 'MEASURED' as const,
    evidenceHref: '/proof#gate-6',
    evidenceTag: 'gate-6-green',
  },
  {
    label: 'Measured downtime across a kill',
    value: '25.2 s',
    note: 'one command; the agent killed with its own daemon',
    badge: 'MEASURED' as const,
    evidenceHref: '/proof#gate-4',
    evidenceTag: 'gate-4-green',
  },
  {
    label: 'A ~14.5 h-old checkpoint woken in',
    value: '14.3 s',
    note: 'COUNT=63 while its living twin read 4841',
    badge: 'MEASURED' as const,
    evidenceHref: '/proof#gate-6',
    evidenceTag: 'gate-6-green',
  },
];
const gates = [
  { tag: 'gate-4-green', href: '/proof#gate-4' },
  { tag: 'gate-6-green', href: '/proof#gate-6' },
];
---
<Product
  slug="sessions"
  title="Sessions · KeepState"
  description="Your agent runs inside a micro-VM KeepState can freeze whole: filesystem, model memory, and tool state captured as one atomic snapshot."
  eyebrow="Sessions"
  headline="Kill it anywhere. Resume anywhere."
  standfirst="Your agent runs inside a micro-VM we can freeze whole. Filesystem, model memory, and tool state are captured as one atomic snapshot, so the world it wakes into and the world it remembers are the same world."
  metrics={metrics}
  evidenceLine="Resume durability and downtime are gated on every release; the raw output is public."
  gates={gates}
  ctaHead="Pull the plug on your own agent."
  ctaBody="Free credits cover a six-hour run and the kill that would have ended it."
>
  <div class="grid gap-11 items-start grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,320px),1fr))]">
    <div>
      <div class="flex items-stretch gap-2.5">
        <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 bg-white border border-sand rounded-4 px-3 py-[18px] text-center">
          <p class="font-mono text-12 text-ink m-0">filesystem</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex-none flex items-center font-mono text-16 text-stone">+</div>
        <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 bg-white border border-sand rounded-4 px-3 py-[18px] text-center">
          <p class="font-mono text-12 text-ink m-0">KV cache</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex-none flex items-center font-mono text-16 text-stone">+</div>
        <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 bg-white border border-sand rounded-4 px-3 py-[18px] text-center">
          <p class="font-mono text-12 text-ink m-0">tool state</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-center py-3.5">
        <span class="block w-px h-[34px] bg-sand"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-blushBg border border-shell rounded-4 p-[22px] flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <span class="w-[9px] h-[9px] bg-claret rotate-45 block"></span>
        <p class="font-mono text-14 text-claret m-0">one atomic checkpoint</p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-14 leading-[1.6] text-slate mt-4 mb-0">Kill it anywhere. Resume anywhere. The world and the memory can never disagree.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="text-16 leading-[1.75] text-slate mt-0 mb-5">A session is a micro-VM we can freeze. The freeze is one write, not three: if the filesystem were captured at one instant and the model memory a beat later, the agent would wake remembering a file that does not exist.</p>
      <p class="text-16 leading-[1.75] text-slate mt-0 mb-6">
        Storage is content-addressed, so aggressive checkpointing stays cheap: 82 checkpoints cost 4,233 MiB where naive copies would cost 80,952 MiB, a 19.1x dedup, and the daemons grew +0 MiB RSS across the 7 h soak that measured it
        <a href="/proof#gate-6" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-12 text-claret no-underline hover:underline ml-1"><span class="w-[5px] h-[5px] bg-claret rotate-45 inline-block"></span>gate-6-green</a>.
        That is why the cadence can be aggressive enough to make a crash boring.
      </p>
      <Terminal session="ks demo" copy="ks demo --kill-at 3m --headless">$ ks demo --kill-at 3m --headless
<span class="text-termMuted">agent up · working on the fixture task</span>
<span class="text-termMuted">kill · the microVM and ksd killed together</span>
<span class="text-blush">resumed · specimen finished the task · measured downtime 25.2 s</span>
<span class="text-termMuted">doctor clean · exit 0</span></Terminal>
      <p class="font-mono text-11 text-taupe mt-2 mb-0">
        the run above is the gate-4 record, not a mock
        <a href="/proof#gate-4" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-11 text-claret no-underline hover:underline ml-1"><span class="w-[5px] h-[5px] bg-claret rotate-45 inline-block"></span>gate-4-green</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Product>
